kage\":\"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/epaxos\",\"Elapsed\":0.011}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));new=r['artifacts'][1];old=r['artifacts'][0];issue=r['review_issues'][0];oldcid=issue['target_id'];cid=[c['id'] for c in r['candidates'] if c['obligation_id']=='O_prepare_value_ballot'][0]\nplan=json.load(open(new['plan_path']));ss=sorted(set(plan['harness']['legality']['source_ids']+plan['monitors'][0]['grounding']['source_ids']))\nitem=dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=ss,rationale='''Reviewed artifact 51278e500469457da64827a253b43d7a v1, its fixed TestAssurancePrepareValueBallot and plan, and raw output/assessment from CheckRun 0485c6c015bc4645a45e0f815f23a3f0. The earlier status check is not used as evidence for this new field comparison.\n\nThe local obligation follows actual interfaces: handlePrepare constructs VBallot from inst.vbal; the Serializable/New/Marshal/Unmarshal chain transports that reply, and handlePrepareReply ranks retained support by the decoded VBallot. The comparison decoded_vballot == sent.producer_vballot encodes precisely that field-preservation responsibility. It does not infer agreement failure or require preserving an unused diagnostic. The source numeric comparison is exact for this int32 field and does not purport to compare command content.\n\nThe fixed constructor initializes N=3,F=1, Thrifty, Dreply and non-durable state consistently with relevant source defaults; reduced capacities are not approached. handlePropose at original owner 1 establishes local value ballot 1, without a test assigning it. The emitted PreAccept reaches peer 2, whose local slot and horizon make it eligible for unresolved-instance recovery. Its original PreAcceptReply is decoded before the subsequent Prepare on the same directed stream but left pending without handler dispatch. This ordering is supported by S_receive: each decoded object is asynchronously queued to its registered message-type channel; S_dispatch selects independent Prepare and PreAcceptReply channels. Thus TCP receipt order does not require processing the earlier reply before Prepare. No global FIFO is relaxed beyond the actual dispatcher. The harness models a permitted finite prefix, not permanent loss of that pending reply. Recovery is scheduled at an eligible slot through startRecoveryForInstance; no numeric timing or eventual-progress conclusion is claimed. The later Prepare with ballot 5 is produced by that handler, not fabricated. The owner has not consumed the pending reply and remains preaccepted. Neither execution nor client reply is required by this local endpoint, and no committed operation or nil reply writer is exercised.\n\nProducer observation is the live local Instance pointer sampled by the sole harness thread after handlePrepare synchronously returns. Source S_prepare changes only bal and copies inst.vbal into its outgoing reply; SendMsg synchronously calls Marshal and Flush. No other writer or handler runs between this emission, sampling and decode. The link previously contained only the consumed PreAccept, so the queued 62 bytes are the new PrepareReply, not unrelated data. Actual New and Unmarshal create/read the receiving object; no supplied expected value modifies it. These ownership and source-call relationships justify the producer sample as the exact value passed to serialization, rather than an unsynchronized cache approximation.\n\nRaw event 3 records producer_vballot=1 and emission for (origin=1,instance=0,acceptor=1,recipient=2,request_ballot=5). Raw event 5 records decoded_vballot=0 with the same independent identity after successful decode; the intervening delivery event contains the same decoded object fields. Identity excludes the compared value ballot. request_ballot identifies the same fixed Prepare request on both sides and is not expected to change during this transport. The sent prerequisite is emission, not the result; the monitor explicitly uses admission_alias=sent. Additional fixed assertions verify decoded sender/instance/promise. Emitted and completed flags occur after the corresponding synchronous actions, not before an awaited condition. Parser reported no errors; comparison and witness are complete; process exited 0 with normal test completion and empty stderr. No workers, sockets or files were started and no shutdown observation is involved.\n\nThe source explains the measured 1-to-0 loss: PrepareReply.Marshal emits no VBallot and Unmarshal never assigns it; New creates fresh zero-valued storage. The pending PreAcceptReply contains VBallot=1 because that distinct codec does include the field, but it cannot populate the separately allocated PrepareReply. The checked discrepancy is therefore local value-history transport. Other report fields remain present and recovery may have independent local evidence; those alternatives limit downstream impact, not the observed field inequality. No issue found is limited to current correspondence, not a universal protocol proof.''',counterevidence=[],limitations=['Only one nonzero original-owner value ballot and one legal finite dispatch schedule are observed.','Actual sockets, execution worker and timer waiting are replaced by deterministic handler scheduling; no timed progress or client completion is asserted.','No PrepareReply is consumed by recovery selection; global consequence and interactions with self-vbal remain open.'],challenged_components=[],report_title='PrepareReply 在线路传输中丢失 value ballot',report_answer='实际提案建立的 value ballot 为 1；同一 Prepare 请求的回复经原实现编码、解码后变为 0。该局部传输缺陷已被执行观测，尚未据此证明恢复决策冲突。')\nresolution=dict(issue_id=issue['id'],source_ids=['S_prepare','S_prepare_codec','S_prepare_new','S_receive','S_recover_select','S_accept','S_wire'],evidence_ids=['60e27f33b9834b7d87fa2fe866557a2e',old['id'],'86de9f55ad84458b9ff6ce6afbac40da'],rationale='The challenged broad interpretation was that Prepare faithfully trans